# Baseline ("unmodified GEM") synthesis: SHRED DSP48E2 / CARRY4 / SRLC32E into
# ordinary AIG gates and flip-flops. This is the Part-D comparison point against
# synth_zenith.ys (which preserves the three primitives as native units).
#
# It is a deliberate mirror of synth_zenith.ys -- SAME passes, SAME order --
# with exactly one difference: the three macros are read as *real synthesizable
# modules* (tests/hetero/behavioral_zenith_macros.sv) instead of as blackboxes
# (aigpdk/zenith_macros.v). Because their bodies are now visible, techmap/abc
# lower the 27x18 multiplier to an adder tree, the CARRY4 to gates, and the
# SRLC32E to a 32-bit shift register -- the graph blow-up the PS asks us to
# avoid by preserving them.
#
# Template file. Use scripts/run_synth_baseline.sh for @@ token expansion.

# Read the three macros as REAL modules (NOT -lib / NOT blackbox).
read_verilog -sv tests/hetero/behavioral_zenith_macros.sv

# Read the user design.
@@GEM_READ@@ @@GEM_DESIGN@@

hierarchy -check -top @@GEM_TOP@@

# Simplify design (identical to synth_zenith.ys)
proc;;
opt_expr; opt_dff; opt_clean

# Keep the original GEM synchronous-memory path functional.
memory -nomap
memory_libmap -lib aigpdk/memlib_yosys.txt -logic-cost-rom 100 -logic-cost-ram 100

# Flatten, then map. Unlike the zenith flow, the macros are ordinary hierarchy
# here, so `flatten` inlines them and the following techmap/abc passes shred
# them into the AIG-PDK cell library.
flatten

techmap
dfflibmap -liberty aigpdk/aigpdk_nomem.lib
opt_clean -purge
abc -liberty aigpdk/aigpdk_nomem.lib
opt_clean -purge
techmap
abc -liberty aigpdk/aigpdk_nomem.lib
opt_clean -purge

# Print cell counts so the benchmark harness can record the AIG graph size.
# NOTE: unlike synth_zenith.ys there is no preservation assertion here -- the
# whole point of the baseline is that the macros do NOT survive.
stat

write_verilog -noattr @@GEM_OUT@@
